00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:03,780
If g and h were different, f keeps them different.

329
00:18:03,780 --> 00:18:06,880
It preserves the information of the entire network.

330
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:09,640
In formal terms, we say the function is left cancelable.

331
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:15,620
And if you apply the exact same logic in reverse, you get the categorical version of surge activity.

332
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:16,820
Let me guess.

333
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:20,160
We look at arrows pointing out of the object instead of in.

334
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:22,020
You are tracking the logic perfectly.

335
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:24,380
It is called an epimorphism.

336
00:18:24,980 --> 00:18:25,540
Epimorphism.

337
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:34,500
If a function f provides such complete coverage of its target space that it can uniquely determine the behavior of any future transformation that follows it,

338
00:18:34,900 --> 00:18:36,020
it's an epimorphism.

339
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:37,260
It is right cancelable.

340
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:43,300
So we have successfully replaced the microscopic study of elements and points with the macroscopic geometry of arrows.

341
00:18:43,500 --> 00:18:43,940
We have.

342
00:18:43,940 --> 00:18:49,340
And speaking of the geometry of arrows, the source material spends pages dissecting commutative diagrams,

